Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.90,0:00:09.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Twenty-five centuries ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.10,0:00:10.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}a man named Zeno proved that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.02,0:00:12.68,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}nothing ever arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.64,0:00:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Hi. I am Jahan,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.72,0:00:19.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}and something impossible\Nhappened to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.38,0:00:21.63,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}Her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.49,0:00:30.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Zeno's argument is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.11,0:00:32.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}To reach any place,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.67,0:00:34.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}you must first cover\Nhalf the distance.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.32,0:00:37.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Then half of what remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.62,0:00:39.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Then half of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.85,0:00:42.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}The halves never run out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.20,0:00:44.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}There is always a remainder,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.18,0:00:46.45,DialogueBright,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur5}and the remainder\Nhas a remainder,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.48,0:00:48.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}so the traveller\Nis stranded forever
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.66,0:00:50.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}in the generous\Nmiddle of the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.88,0:00:56.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}For centuries, this was treated\Nas a puzzle about motion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.32,0:00:58.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}I submit it is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.34,0:00:60.00,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}a puzzle about waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.14,0:01:03.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Here is the evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.30,0:01:05.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}A gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.69,0:01:06.69,DialogueBright,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur5}A street.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.17,0:01:09.13,DialogueBright,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur5}Eleven metres of tarmac.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.63,0:01:11.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}The hazard lights ticking.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.53,0:01:16.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}And you, still somewhere\Nin the first half,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.11,0:01:17.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}which makes you,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.37,0:01:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}by every known law\Nof logic, impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.79,0:01:24.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}I have watched this\Nhundreds of times.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.63,0:01:31.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Mathematicians eventually\Nrescued us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.08,0:01:34.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Add every half\Ntogether, they said:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.59,0:01:36.67,DialogueBright,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur5}a half, a quarter, an eighth,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.72,0:01:38.84,DialogueBright,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur5}and the total is exactly one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.04,0:01:42.86,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}The infinite fits\Ninside a finite walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.24,0:01:44.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}How reassuring.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.35,0:01:49.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}But the sum only\Nmeasures how far.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.14,0:01:52.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}It cannot say what\Nthe in-between is like:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.12,0:01:54.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}the hair in your face\Nat the quarter mark,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.94,0:01:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}the half-smile you wear\Nwhen you think nobody's watching.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.45,0:02:07.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Heraclitus said no one steps\Ninto the same river twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.80,0:02:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Nobody gets into\Nthe same car twice, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.35,0:02:15.41,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}Hundred arrivals,\Nhundred different women,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.45,0:02:17.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}and every single\None of them you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.26,0:02:33.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Diogenes answered Zeno\Nby standing up and walking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.46,0:02:36.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}You answer him every time\Nby getting in.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.68,0:02:42.58,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}Love is not the proof.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.49,0:02:48.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}Love is the practical,\Nslightly awkward,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.79,0:02:51.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}repeated action\Nof putting the hazards on
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.27,0:02:54.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}and sitting there\Nwhile she crosses the distance
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.57,0:02:57.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)\blur3.5}that logic says\Ncan never be finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.46,0:03:01.71,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}I am here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.58,0:03:06.99,Emphasis,,0,0,0,,{\fad(320,260)\blur3.5}No hurry.
